    {
      "external_id": "C11-PHY-CH2-2.3-CHARACTERISTICS-OF-CROSS-PRODUCT",
      "chapter": "pk-punjab/xi/physics/c11-phy/ch2",
      "topic": "pk-punjab/xi/physics/c11-phy/ch2/u-characteristics-of-cross-product",
      "title": "Characteristics of Cross Product",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "e2c5c034-041b-5340-9823-5e3c8c88a07c",
          "pdf_from": 25,
          "pdf_to": 25,
          "note": "Characteristics of Cross Product: a main subheading of 2.3 Product of two vectors, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 25-25."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "Since A⃗ x B⃗ is not the same as B⃗ x A⃗, the cross product is non commutative. so,"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\vec{A}\\times\\vec{B} \\neq \\vec{B}\\times\\vec{A}",
            "text_alt": "A⃗ × B⃗ ≠ B⃗ × A⃗"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "The cross product of two perpendicular vectors (θ = 90°) has maximum magnitude"
            ],
            "start": 2
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\vec{A}\\times\\vec{B} = AB\\sin 90^\\circ\\,\\hat{n} = AB\\,\\hat{n}",
            "text_alt": "A⃗ × B⃗ = AB sin 90° n̂ = AB n̂"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "The cross product of two parallel vectors is null vector, because for such vectors θ = 0° or 180°, Hence,"
            ],
            "start": 3
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\vec{A}\\times\\vec{B} = AB\\sin 0^\\circ\\,\\hat{n} = 0 \\quad\\text{or}\\quad \\vec{A}\\times\\vec{B} = AB\\sin 180^\\circ\\,\\hat{n} = 0",
            "text_alt": "A⃗ × B⃗ = AB sin 0° n̂ = 0 or A⃗ × B⃗ = AB sin 180° n̂ = 0"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "As a consequence A⃗ x A⃗ = 0 (θ = 0°)"
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": true,
            "items": [
              "The magnitude of A⃗ x B⃗ is equal to the area of the parallelogram formed with A⃗ and B⃗ as two adjacent sides Fig.2.4 (d)."
            ],
            "start": 4
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
